cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this paper or its data set, please cite it as below."
title: "Task-specific fine-tuning of a small AI model for GMP deviation triage: effects of LoRA fine-tuning and switchable building blocks on classification accuracy and data integrity"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Cancemi
    given-names: Alessandro
date-released: "2026-11-27"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tangozwo-max/pharma40research/tree/main/papers/2026-01-deviation-triage-small-model"
url: "https://pharma40.de/research"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A small open-weight model (Qwen3-8B) with five switchable building blocks and LoRA fine-tuning, tested on a
  synthetic data set of 4,286 deviation notes from 150 cause families. Code-side grounding removed invented values;
  a LoRA adapter raised macro-F1 on unseen cause families from 94.3 % to 98.2 %. Working paper, not peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - small language models
  - LoRA
  - structured extraction
  - grounding
  - data integrity
  - GMP
  - deviation management
